From 0baf46c629ea96c27129b8d7aeb3fb27649e070f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:24:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] rdna-boosts: block 10: slab, fusion dispatcher, async
 input ring (infrastructure)

The infrastructure half of the old block 10.  qwen4exp, QSA and the
hyper-connection ops now live in their own block (11); this block is what they
are built on, and it no longer references them.

Contents:

- The movable-boundary slab and its arena (ggml-cuda-slab.cu,
  ggml-cuda-arena.cu, ggml-cuda-vmm.h, ggml-cuda-moe-cache-hooks.cu): one VMM
  reserve per device split by a movable boundary -- compute below, MoE arena
  above, no HIP call at runtime.  Plus the narrow-band learning, the wide-phase
  auxiliary region, pool-wide routing, and the slab transient absorption.
- The fusion dispatcher (ggml-cuda-try-fuse.cu): the matcher arms moved out of
  ggml-cuda.cu, with every arm implemented inside the kernel TU that owns it.
- The async graph-input ring: batched uploads + lazy done event (PR #182), the
  r90 snapshot fix (the scheduler's set_tensor_async path is used for a CPU
  split's output, which the next ubatch rewrites), default-on, and the per-origin
  (per host thread) ordering state of issue #201.
- Rope/FWHT fusions: M-ROPE and IMROPE in the RMS_NORM + MUL + ROPE (+ FWHT)
  matcher, BF16 SET_ROWS kept off the 5-op fusion, the q8_0 K/V cache writes
  folded into the rope + FWHT kernel, and the paired GDN q/k norms.
- GDN / attention-gate decode fusions: the BF16 alpha/beta pair with
  softplus(alpha + dt) * a in one mul_mat_vec_f launch (with the r108
  multi-sequence fix and its model-free regression test), the q/k norm pair in
  the direct conv kernel, the attention gate's row-strided view read in place by
  the gate -> Q8_1 kernel, the GDN output norm inside the gate kernel, and
  GGML_CUDA_GDN_TAIL (the sequential tail that writes the rollback snapshots).
- MMB and the HC16 BF16 streams: the per-context MMB state (two contexts
  interleaving must not share the activation cache or the marks), the BF16
  activation copies, DOWN16, and the graph-optimize marking passes.
- The MoE/MMQ decode fusions: mmvq-moe (the dedicated MoE multi-token kernel),
  the gate+up pair fold, silu(gate)*up into the mmq quantize, the dual-output
  matmul, the MoE down fold, and the weighted-down reduction.
- The verify-band arch extension: RDNA3_0 joins RDNA4 in the Q8_1 pre-quantize
  predicate and in the direct GDN conv.
- Meta/scheduler/allocator: the split-state refusals for a straddling split,
  the two-pass graph-optimize protocol (allocs_only / marks_only), graph-memory
  generations so a graph is recaptured when the pool / FA staging / H2D ring
  memory it captured is freed -- including the slab work-boundary shrink of
  issue #187 -- the KV prefill pad (LLAMA_KV_N_PAD_PREFILL), and the FA accuracy
  instrument (LLAMA_TEST_OP_NMSE / LLAMA_TEST_SEED).
- bf16 RoPE destinations (TODO #83): the missing NORMAL/NEOX bf16
  instantiations, so -ctk bf16 -ctv bf16 prefill does not abort in rope.cu.

Env-read hygiene (no behaviour change): resolve GGML_CUDA_GDN_CHUNKED /
GGML_CUDA_GDN_CHUNKED_BF16 and the GDN_DBG_SKIP_* diagnostics once into values
rather than caching the getenv() pointer: the MSVC CRT returns a buffer that the
next getenv() call overwrites, so a cached pointer is unsafe on Windows.

Build fix: the GGML_CUDA_WORK_ALLOC_DEBUG read in llama_context::graph_reserve
lives in src/ (not linked against the CUDA common.cuh), so it uses a local
static instead of the CUDA helper.

Split note (r109): this commit plus block 11 carries exactly the tree the old
block 10 carried -- the net set is unchanged.  What moved to block 11 is the
qwen4exp model graph, the QSA/indexer ops and their kernels, the
hyper-connection ops, the managed lazy reader and the keys-only indexer cache,
i.e. everything that exists only because of that architecture.  The pieces of
the old block 10 that exist for qwen4exp but are implemented inside a general
kernel TU (the GDN gate/beta fusion, the HC16 MMB BF16 streams, the qwen4exp
weighted-down reduction, the PLE conv fusion) stay here with the TU that owns
them; the HC_BLK16/RES16 marking pass and the indexer relu-sum alloc-dep moved
to block 11 with the matchers they call.

Windows HIP build (issue #217): the tables-registration slack guard uses the int64_t min/max helpers
block 09 defines instead of `std::min<int64_t>`/`std::max<int64_t>`.  With HIP on Windows (clang + the
MSVC STL) clang's force-included `cuda_wrappers/algorithm` and the MSVC STL `<utility>` each define an
inline `std::min<long long>` (`int64_t` is `__int64` there, and the `enable_if` that makes clang's
version win overload resolution is not part of the mangled name), so a translation unit that
instantiates both fails to codegen with "definition with same mangled name".  Behaviour is unchanged.

Amended (r132): the block-10 arms of the Q8_1 cache fix that block 08 introduces.  The fused GLU -> Q8_1 site's
key walk stops at the first pointer change (the fused write is keyed by the matmul's src1, and must not take the
root's entry for an offset view), and both of this block's gated-q8_1 launch arms -- the fused norm+gate kernel
and the GLU write -- validate their sources with q8_1_src_range_ok() before launching.  From PR #218 (@slavap);
the rule and the validation are recorded with block 08.

Co-authored-by: Slava P. <slavap@users.noreply.github.com>
